File Index

/DevicesPanel.test.tsx
Purpose: List rendering with audience + dates, the revoked-collapse toggle, single and bulk revoke behind confirms, and — pinned separately because it is the one that would silently mislead — a failed load surfacing an error rather than rendering an empty list as "no devices". Both confirm-dismissed paths assert nothing was called: revocation is not undoable, so a stray click must cost nothing.

/DevicesPanel.tsx
Purpose: The enrolled-device list and its two revoke actions (one device / all devices), rendered inside KeysPage rather than as its own nav section — keys and devices are different axes of the same access question (a key is per-service across all devices; a device is per-browser across all services) and users pick the wrong one when they only see one. No create action and no show-once secret: enrolment happens in the consumer app because it requires a live hub session, the private key is non-extractable, and re-enrolling from the browser IS the rotate. Revoked rows are permanent tombstones server-side, so they stay collapsed behind a Show revoked (n) toggle. Deliberately NO "this device" badge — the device key lives in the enrolling ORIGIN's IndexedDB (build.shatteredarchive.dev), which the hub cannot read, so the badge would be a guess; labels default to "Chrome on Windows" at enrolment instead. Carries the lost-laptop caveat in the UI, not just the docs: a thief holds the browser's live hub session too and can silently re-enrol, so a password change (which bumps the account epoch and kills every session AND enrolment) is the actual remedy.
